  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta =\\frac{5}{3},$ where $\\theta =m\u2220B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ adjacent to $\u2220B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3} & =\\frac{AC}{18} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\cdot 18 & =AC \\\\ AC & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =270.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
